libarchive-rust is a port of libarchive (https://github.com/libarchive/libarchive)
to Rust. Like libarchive, the distribution as a whole is subject to the
BSD-2-Clause license in LICENSE.

Each source file carries its own copyright and licensing statement at its
beginning; those statements are controlling. A module ported from an upstream
file keeps that file's statement unchanged. The following summarizes the
exceptions, mirroring upstream's COPYING:

* In whole or in part subject to a 3-clause UC Regents copyright:
    src/read/filter/compress.rs   (archive_read_support_filter_compress.c)
    src/write/filter/compress.rs  (archive_write_add_filter_compress.c)

* In the public domain:
    src/parse_date.rs             (archive_parse_date.c)
    src/ppmd.rs, src/ppmd7.rs, src/ppmd8.rs  (Igor Pavlov's PPMd code)

* Triple-licensed under CC0 1.0 Universal, OpenSSL or Apache 2.0:
    src/blake2s_ref.rs, src/blake2sp_ref.rs

* deflate/ is a port of zlib 1.2.12's compressor and is under the zlib
  license (deflate/LICENSE), marked as an altered version.

* Patched copies of third-party crates under vendor/ keep their own
  licenses; see the LICENSE files there:
    vendor/miniz_oxide   MIT, Zlib or Apache-2.0
    vendor/lzma-rust2    Apache-2.0
    vendor/ruzstd        MIT

* Crates fetched from crates.io (see Cargo.lock) are under their own
  licenses, mostly MIT or Apache-2.0; xxhash-rust is BSL-1.0.

* upstream/libarchive is a git submodule of the upstream project, used
  only as the test oracle; see its own COPYING.
